All 15 tests pass. Here's what was fixed across the 3 source files:

**`src/auth.py`** — 2 bugs:
- `has_permission`: case-sensitive `in` check → `.lower()` comparison via generator
- `is_admin_or_owner`: `and` → `or` (admin and owner are independent grants, not conjunctive)

**`src/inventory.py`** — 4 bugs:
- `__init__`: mutable default `{}` → `None` + fresh dict per instance (two inventories were sharing storage)
- `add`: assignment (`= qty`) → accumulation (`= ... + qty`)
- `reserve`: `>=` → `>` (reserving exactly the available amount should succeed)
- `release`: added validation — raises `ValueError` when releasing more than reserved

**`src/text_utils.py`** — 3 bugs:
- `slugify`: added `.lower()` on alphanumeric characters
- `slugify`: `str.replace("--", "-")` only collapsed one adjacent pair → `re.sub(r"-+", "-", ...)` collapses all runs
- `truncate`: `text[:max_len] + suffix` overflowed → `text[:max_len - len(suffix)] + suffix`
